# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, stops host-built
# artefacts leaking into the image.
#
# node_modules matters most: this repo is developed on Windows, and copying
# those binaries over the ones installed inside Alpine gives a broken Prisma
# engine that fails at runtime rather than at build time.

node_modules
.next
.git
.github
.vercel

# Secrets must never enter an image layer — they stay in the platform's env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Database dumps hold real customer data.
backups

# Local tooling and test output that the runtime has no use for.
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
.claude
docs
README.md
